92186436314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436329 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436329 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436329 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436329 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fb776df8-d18c-56c6-b0af-71e18ee9b2ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436330 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436330 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159624" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436330 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436330 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y{e}^{x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436330 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ea23849-68e0-52dc-ba91-b8da7ebd925a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436330 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}+y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y})+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot {e}^{y}+{e}^{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436331 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436331 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159609" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436331 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436331 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2{x}^{5}{e}^{y},$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436331 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90392678-f725-5c12-933c-87fa3256c47c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436331 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2{x}^{5}{e}^{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{5}{e}^{y}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-2{e}^{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{5}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})-2{e}^{y}\\cdot (5{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}-10{x}^{4}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{1}-10\\cdot {1}^{4}\\cdot {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-10\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-30\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436332 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436326 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436332 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159575" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436332 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436332 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)={x}^{y},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436332 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9785714b-27e4-57d0-bac5-65edf8d118a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436332 #edb/ref 1074 "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={x}^{y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=(x+h)^{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(x+h)^{y}-{x}^{y}}{h}).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436333 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436333 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436333 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ given that $f(x,y)=3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y-x{y}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436333 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ca64fedb-1539-5dab-a00d-8a624f81d8c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436333 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y-x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-x\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1+{y}^{2}}-2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436334 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436334 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159576" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436334 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436334 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2}),$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436334 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ea65f87f-49a7-5b8c-93db-0d61d7663ef3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436334 #edb/ref 1074 "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2}),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+h-{y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+h-{y}^{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})}{h}).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436335 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436335 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159572" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436335 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436335 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436335 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fab082ec-08e1-574d-8102-367e3c718114" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436335 #edb/ref 1074 "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡((x+h)y).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡((x+h)y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}{h}).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
